{"id":"nursing-home-chains","title":"Nursing-home chains: revenue, profit, related balances and staffing over time","question":"For each chain with three or more Bay Area nursing homes, how have revenue per resident day, profit, balances with related companies and nurse hours moved since 2019?","finding":"14 chains have three or more Bay Area homes in the State reports; the largest is PACS Group with 31 ($738.4 million of revenue and $119.2 million of net income in 2025, $436.0 million owed to its homes by related parties). Across all 183 homes, revenue per resident day rose from $400 in 2019 to $591, net income from 3.8% to 12.9% of revenue, and nurse hours per resident day in the State reports went from 3.98 to 4.17. The chain with the largest share of its homes' assets owed by related parties is PACS Group (78%).","how":"The State financial reports of the previous screen, added up by the chain each home belongs to in the federal enrollment file of October 2026. Money columns are for each chain's latest report year; 2019 columns use the same homes. Nurse hours in the State report are productive hours of registered nurses, licensed vocational nurses and nurse assistants, employed and temporary, divided by resident days. \"Payroll file\" is the middle home's figure in the federal daily staffing file for the latest four quarters. Changed hands counts homes with a change of ownership recorded by Medicare since 2019. Citations and penalties are State actions from 2019 to June 2024.","limits":"Chain membership is today's, applied to every earlier year, so a home bought in 2023 carries its previous owner's results into the chain's 2019 column; the \"changed hands\" column shows where that matters. A chain's home office charges each home for shared services, which moves profit between the home and the chain: a low or high margin at the homes says little about the group as a whole. Revenue per day rises with Medi-Cal rate increases and with a sicker, shorter-stay mix of residents. The two staffing measures are built differently and should be compared within a column, not across. Reports since 2023 are as submitted.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"chain","t":"Chain (federal file)","type":"text"},{"k":"homes","t":"Bay Area homes","type":"int"},{"k":"sfHomes","t":"In San Francisco","type":"int"},{"k":"year","t":"Report year","type":"year"},{"k":"revenue","t":"Revenue","type":"usd"},{"k":"netIncome","t":"Net income","type":"usd"},{"k":"margin","t":"Net income share","type":"pct"},{"k":"margin2019","t":"Same, 2019","type":"pct"},{"k":"relatedNet","t":"Owed by related parties, net","type":"usd"},{"k":"relatedShare","t":"Share of assets","type":"pct"},{"k":"adminPerDay","t":"Administration per resident day","type":"usd"},{"k":"leasePerDay","t":"Lease and rent per resident day","type":"usd"},{"k":"revPerDay","t":"Revenue per resident day","type":"usd"},{"k":"revPerDay2019","t":"Same, 2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"hours","t":"Nurse hours per resident day, State report","type":"int"},{"k":"hours2019","t":"Same, 2019","type":"int"},{"k":"payrollHours","t":"Nurse hours, federal payroll file","type":"int"},{"k":"changedHands","t":"Homes that changed hands since 2019","type":"int"},{"k":"citations","t":"State citations and penalties since 2019","type":"int"},{"k":"hoursPenalties","t":"Of which nursing-hours penalties","type":"int"},{"k":"penalties","t":"Penalty dollars","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"chain":"PACS Group","homes":31,"sfHomes":4,"year":2025,"revenue":738370949,"netIncome":119229623,"margin":0.161,"margin2019":0.043,"relatedNet":436030162,"relatedShare":0.782,"adminPerDay":144,"leasePerDay":47,"revPerDay":682,"revPerDay2019":432,"hours":4.15,"hours2019":3.83,"payrollHours":4.12,"changedHands":13,"citations":35,"hoursPenalties":19,"penalties":580000},{"chain":"Generations Healthcare","homes":8,"sfHomes":1,"year":2025,"revenue":185297553,"netIncome":22165917,"margin":0.12,"margin2019":0.057,"relatedNet":141116761,"relatedShare":0.565,"adminPer